// ================= MIREFEN ON THE MUSHROOM CAPS (Book 1, Sporeholm) =================
// "Little round huts sit on the glowing caps... wobbly rope bridges swoop and sway between the mushrooms, with planks so far apart
//  you can see the misty swamp far below. Ladders made of vines run up and down the stalks. On the tallest mushroom, right in the
//  middle, sits a wide, flat, open platform with no huts: the gathering place where the Spore Choir sings."
// B2 (lane homes) and B3 (village centre) are lifted onto giant mushroom caps: one cap per corner block of homes and shops, a round
// cap at each crossing (the tallest, in B3, is the Choir Platform). The streets between become misty swamp far below, crossed by
// rope bridges; the streets that lead out of the village become great root stairs winding down to the ground.
// Everything here is authored on the tile grid (a, b) and mapped through the terrain warp, so caps, stalks and bridges line up.
